(
 'Prints a list with all files captured in a stash, including untracked files.'
 ''
 'If no argument is specified, it attempts to find open Cider/acre project(s).'
 'If it finds one, it will act on it.'
 'If it finds multiple open Cider/acre projects, it will ask the user which one to act on.'
 'If it does not find any open projects it will ask the user whether it should act on the current directory.'
 'If the user negates the question an error will be thrown.'
 ''
 'You may specify the number of the stash you are interested in as argument, or as second argument.'
 'If you do not specify such an argument it defaults to 0 (the latest stash).'
 ''
 'By default, a two-column matrix is returned with APL names (if any) in the second column.'
 'You can suppress this by specifying the flag -noAPLnames. Then a vector of filenames is returned.'
)
